ttdbserverd: keep the record lengths getISAMFileInfo() set

Both _Tt_isam_file constructors open (or build) the ISAM file, call
getISAMFileInfo() -- which sets maxRecordLength from isindexinfo()'s
di_recsize and minRecordLength from isreclen -- and then, as their last
two statements, set both back to 0.

Every buffer sized from them is therefore empty.  readRecord() does

    _Tt_string record_buffer(maxRecordLength);   // malloc(0 + 1)
    isread(fileDescriptor, (char *)record_buffer, mode);

and isread() copies a whole record (fcb->minreclen octets, more with a
variable-length tail) into that one-byte allocation, running straight
over the heap header of whatever was allocated next.  In _amread() that
is the `oldcurpos` byte array it _bytearr_dup()s immediately afterwards,
so the overrun is caught when it is freed:

    free <- _bytearr_free <- _amread <- isread
         <- _Tt_isam_file::readRecord <- setFileProperties
         <- _tt_create_file_1 <- _tt_dbserver_prog_1 <- svc_run

On substrate the overwritten header's `prev` link read 0xffffffff and
rpc.ttdbserver died with SIGSEGV in libc's coalesce_block() on the first
tt_create_file RPC of every CDE login, with no ToolTalk file properties
ever stored.  getEmptyRecord() and getFullRecord() size their records
from the same two members, so their buffers were zero-length too.

The zeroing was evidently meant as initialisation; do it first, before
the file is opened, so the members are still defined when the open
fails and getISAMFileInfo()'s values survive when it succeeds.

Verified on substrate: headless CDE login through sgreet, 4 of 4 runs
crashed before; with this change rpc.ttdbserver survives, and
/TT_DB/property_table.{rec,var} grow as the properties are written
(the .var file stayed at 0 octets before).

diff --git a/lib/tt/bin/ttdbserverd/tt_isam_file.C b/lib/tt/bin/ttdbserverd/tt_isam_file.C
index 5cb64f2b..37c18495 100644
--- a/lib/tt/bin/ttdbserverd/tt_isam_file.C
+++ b/lib/tt/bin/ttdbserverd/tt_isam_file.C
@@ -45,6 +45,8 @@ _Tt_isam_file::_Tt_isam_file (const _Tt_string &file, int mode)
   setTtISAMFileDefaults();
   fileName = file;
   fileMode = mode;
+  maxRecordLength = 0;
+  minRecordLength = 0;

   if ((fileDescriptor = cached_isopen(file, mode)) != -1) {
     getISAMFileInfo();
@@ -52,9 +54,6 @@ _Tt_isam_file::_Tt_isam_file (const _Tt_string &file, int mode)
   else {
     getStatusInfo();
   }
-
-  maxRecordLength = 0;
-  minRecordLength = 0;
 }

 _Tt_isam_file
@@ -67,6 +66,8 @@ _Tt_isam_file
   setTtISAMFileDefaults();
   fileName = file;
   fileMode = mode;
+  maxRecordLength = 0;
+  minRecordLength = 0;

   if ((fileDescriptor = cached_isopen(file, mode)) == -1) {
     newFlag = TRUE;
@@ -85,9 +86,6 @@ _Tt_isam_file
     currentRecordLength = -1;
     currentRecordNumber = -1;
   }
-
-  maxRecordLength = 0;
-  minRecordLength = 0;
 }

